{"assertionId":"E-BL1-10","captureTimestamp":"2026-10-11T00:27:10Z","claim":"Variant example sources and assets contain no external URL or remote asset and no literal colour value, and every asset that is not Mux-authored has a license and disclosure record (the blocks have no asset files). An independent review finds no third-party brand logo or mark, no real person's name or likeness, and only generic Mux-authored copy in each block.","environment":{"architecture":"arm64","browsers":{"chrome":"Google Chrome 154.0.8037.99","playwrightBuilds":["chromium_headless_shell-1208","firefox-1538","webkit-2336"],"playwrightCore":"1.62.1"},"node":"v24.19.0","pnpm":"10.33.0","runnerOs":"macOS 27.0"},"evidenceKind":"content-scan-and-independent-review","observations":{"review":{"advisoryDisposition":"Not fixed by the capture: changing a block source changes its tree and needs a new review of that block. The advisory lines are optional follow-ups for a later block change, not a failed finding.","advisoryLines":["- Both changed lines were read against the c1e5c437 advisory each answers (see Per-block findings). The other 24 pattern files are byte-identical to c1e5c437; they were still re-read and re-scanned.","- **Limits:** the review did not run the compiler, `pnpm generate`, the test suites, the browser suites, the capture script, or the docs site. Browser test sources were read, not run, where an advisory depends on them. The reviewer has no copy of the source demos; freshness was checked only against the demo data the earlier reviews list, and the only copy changed since c1e5c437 reuses titles the C","- c1e5c437 advisory, \"Disabled A …\" prefix and differing phrasing between variants: **resolved.**","- Advisory (carried forward, still present): \"Start free and upgrade when you need more.\" (`columns.tsx:127`) carries no in-block placeholder marker. The record calls the prices placeholders (`artifact.json:68`), and `SCOPE-NONGOAL-008` covers them, so this is acceptable.","- Advisory (carried forward, still present, low): \"Card selected state: Card.Root has none\" (`artifact.json:70`). It is true: `packages/react/src` is unchanged since c1e5c437, where `Card.Root` renders a plain `div` with no selected state. It would go stale only if `Card.Root` gains one.","- c1e5c437 advisory, aria-sort verb: **resolved.** The line now reads \"Sortable column headers sort on click, Enter, or Space, and set aria-sort to ascending, descending, or none.\" (`catalog/patterns/company-records/artifact.json:67`), the suggested wording. It matches \"sets aria-expanded\" in `workspace-navigation/artifact.json:62`, names an ARIA attribute, and claims no AT behaviour.","- Advisory (carried forward, still present): \"Generic Supply\" (`sortable.tsx:11`) shares the common noun \"Supply\" with an earlier mock's \"Northwind Supply\". It is not reuse.","- Advisory (carried forward, still present): the forced-colours note (`artifact.json:71`) is a CSS mechanism note, backed by an emulated forced-colours browser test (`packages/react/test/browser/pattern-company-records.test.mjs`, unchanged since c1e5c437), not by a run in a real forced-colours environment. It is not an AT or support claim.","- Advisory (carried forward, still present): \"Review the draft outline\" (`filter-bar.tsx:6`, `status-buttons.tsx:6`) shares \"Review\" and \"draft\" with an earlier mock's \"Review the menu draft\". It is not reuse.","- Advisory (carried forward, no change needed): \"complementary landmark\", \"navigation landmark\", and \"a dialog named Navigation\" (`artifact.json:61,65`) name ARIA roles that follow from DOM structure. They claim no tested or supported AT behaviour.","- Advisory (carried forward, still present): the forced-colours note (`artifact.json:66`) is backed by an emulated forced-colours test (`packages/react/test/browser/pattern-workspace-navigation.test.mjs`, unchanged since c1e5c437), not by a real forced-colours run. It is not an AT or support claim.","- Advisory (carried forward, still present): the `Switch` icon (`foldable.tsx:19`) has the same geometry as Lucide's `chevrons-up-down`. It is two plain chevrons, ISC-licensed and listed in `packages/react/NOTICE`, not a mark, and Decision 0029 records Lucide as Mux UI's default icon set. Importing the Lucide icon, or noting that the path follows it, would make the provenance exact.","- Advisory (carried forward, still present): the Cmd or Ctrl plus B fold shortcut (`shortcut=\"b\"`, line 148; `artifact.json:62`) matches the source demo's toggle. It is a common convention and a behaviour, not copy, and the block renders no shortcut hint.","- Advisory (carried forward, still present): of the seven blocks this one is closest to a page shell. It stays one region because the main pane is only a placeholder (`foldable.tsx:154-161`). Filling that pane with page content would move it toward the page templates that item 6 excludes."],"artifact":{"path":"tests/evidence/bl1/artifacts/E-BL1-10-content-review.md","sha256":"sha256:0bd10f47fd0bcee8374ced605110bd7f9a824030141a6b3a2b325821adb6701a"},"blocks":["account-settings","company-records","marketing-hero","poster-grid","pricing-plans","task-filters","workspace-navigation"],"comparison":{"changedPathCount":0,"changedPaths":[],"changedPathsTruncated":false,"equalTrees":true,"proofToolsChangedSinceReviewed":[],"sourceTree":"415c23b15a5740fb1bce2bc5f3b90000acb9c6db"},"limits":"The reviewer read the sources and rules; it did not run the compiler scanner, the tests, or the docs site. The scanner and the tests ran above.","raw":{"bytes":25155,"retained":false,"sha256":"sha256:a0c2479d6e600ad3f519240a1269a2c4dc1035c8f0f894f97eb71c0a63406c95"},"reviewedRevision":"1899324c8aed2d94a6324c4656d2149af5571f39","reviewedRevisionDiffersFromSource":false,"reviewedRevisionInMainHistory":true,"reviewedTree":"415c23b15a5740fb1bce2bc5f3b90000acb9c6db","reviewer":"independent read-only reviewer agent (Claude Opus 5.5), not the authoring agents.","sanitization":{"replacements":{"home":1,"repositoryRoot":0,"temporary":0},"rule":"the record is retained as the reviewer wrote it except that local paths are rewritten: the repository root to <repo>, temporary directories to <tmp>, and home directories to <home>; replacements counts each"},"verdict":"pass","verdictText":"**Pass.** All seven blocks meet the E-BL1-10 content assertions at `1899324c`:\n\n- no third-party brand or mark;\n- no real person's name or likeness;\n- only generic Mux-authored copy, with no distinctive reuse from a source demo;\n- no external URL or remote asset;\n- no literal colour;\n- no unlicensed asset;\n- every import is a declared participant;\n- the bounded-section test passes for every block;\n- no record or visible prose claims accessibility, testing, support, or compliance, names a screen reader, or cites WCAG.\n\nThe #266 copy changes are generic and Mux-authored and introduce no claim. The virtualized disabled titles agree with the disabled cards (90 of 1,000, each titled \"Disabled\", no enabled card so titled), the comment matches the code, and the titles match the CSS-grid variant word for word. #263's `category` field lands on five component records that no block uses and is navigation metadata, not rendered copy. `packages/react/src` is unchanged since c1e5c437, so no participant's default placeholder or label changed.\n\n**Resolved by #266:** the \"Disabled A …\" phrasing and the differing disabled-title phrasing between the poster-grid variants (`poster-grid/examples/react/virtualized.tsx:21-31`, matching `css-grid.tsx:10,15`); and the \"report … through aria-sort\" verb (`company-records/artifact.json:67`).\n\nNo failure. The remaining advisories are optional follow-ups and do not block this verdict:\n\n- Carried: the unmarked pricing offer copy (`pricing-plans/examples/react/columns.tsx:127`).\n- Carried, low: the stale-prone \"Card.Root has none\" (`pricing-plans/artifact.json:70`), true today.\n- Carried: the forced-colours notes (`company-records/artifact.json:71`, `workspace-navigation/artifact.json:66`), which emulated tests back but no real forced-colours run does.\n- Carried: the generic-word echoes \"Generic Supply\" and \"Review the draft outline\".\n- Carried: the Lucide-identical `Switch` chevron glyph (`workspace-navigation/examples/react/foldable.tsx:19`).\n- Carried: the shared Cmd or Ctrl plus B convention with the source demo.\n- Carried: workspace-navigation is the block closest to a page shell, so its main pane should stay a placeholder."},"reviewCoverage":{"rows":[{"block":"account-settings","key":{"blockTree":"6f367c30ade16b679a1b08541f7c8804fc87f166","participants":[{"component":"muxui:component:button","tree":"ddb4f51d31b02fbf77c73e217bde2232b6280998"},{"component":"muxui:component:form","tree":"058c6b74814d47549b9979188007333715e6514c"},{"component":"muxui:component:select","tree":"9791088d21716cd2324ed6976d0b1cc7cca36b44"},{"component":"muxui:component:separator","tree":"32ae2a8609a5bd11adb849b53d136a96aed925e0"},{"component":"muxui:component:switch","tree":"745ce27588dda2e82113f5f3d850e7a33058eadf"},{"component":"muxui:component:text","tree":"7df0a020dad64cb54ab3bef1d0bb7aefb50bb482"},{"component":"muxui:component:text-field","tree":"2c2df369f97a02be9d72714468d2ad104ee1a783"}],"reactRuntime":{"digest":"sha256:b534fc1cb6f7eb6a354822c304a05a6cdcfecb52cbe7071f8ae244f9fe098a4c","excluded":["packages/react/src/r1-contracts.mjs","packages/react/src/r1-deferred-evidence.mjs","packages/react/src/publish-guard.mjs"],"files":76,"root":"packages/react/src"}},"review":{"artifact":{"path":"tests/evidence/bl1/artifacts/E-BL1-10-content-review.md","sha256":"sha256:0bd10f47fd0bcee8374ced605110bd7f9a824030141a6b3a2b325821adb6701a"},"keyAtReviewedRevision":{"blockTree":"6f367c30ade16b679a1b08541f7c8804fc87f166","participants":[{"component":"muxui:component:button","tree":"ddb4f51d31b02fbf77c73e217bde2232b6280998"},{"component":"muxui:component:form","tree":"058c6b74814d47549b99791880073